      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-298351",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/15/152d1e2c658369ebc546fa3eace344a651f10aa55b883d1652d56d4d917edd21.png)\n\nTwo households recorded the number of fruits each family member ate per day during a certain period. The information for Household A is summarized in the dot plot above, where each dot represents the number of fruits eaten by a certain household member on a particular day. Household B had a mean number of servings equal to $4.2$.\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nHousehold A's mean number of daily servings is\n{{field-1}}.\n\nThe mean for Household B is\n{{field-2}}\nthe mean for Household A.\n\nA comparison of the means suggests members of\n{{field-3}}\nconsumed more fruit per day.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
